findings.body:
`True` isn't defined in JavaScript or TypeScript:

::diff{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="130-144"}

`tsc` will reject this with "Cannot find name 'True'", so `web` type-checking fails.

If the code is shipped anyway, every keystroke that leaves the editor holding valid JSON runs `handlePayloadChange(...)` and then throws `ReferenceError: True is not defined` inside Monaco's change handler. That is the exact path the PR is trying to enable.

The return value isn't used: `CodeEditor` types `onChange` as `(value: string) => void`. The parsed `v` is unused too.

::suggestion{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="130-144"}
  const handleJSONSchemaChange = useCallback((value: string) => {
    if (value == null || value.trim() === '') {
      handlePayloadChange('json_schema')(undefined)
      return
    }
    try {
      JSON.parse(value)
      handlePayloadChange('json_schema')(value)
    }
    catch {
      // keep last valid value
    }
  }, [handlePayloadChange])

`normalizedJsonSchema` is computed and never used. `payloadToSave` repeats the same logic inline. The parsed `v` in `handleJSONSchemaChange` is also unused. `jsonObjectWrap` in `config.ts` is still exported but nothing imports it anymore. The repo's ESLint config will probably flag the unused locals.

::diff{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="248-258"}

The comment also says "if the input type is jsonObject", but the stripping applies to every type. That's harmless, but the comment is misleading.

::suggestion{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="249-258"}
    const jsonSchemaValue = tempPayload.json_schema
    const isSchemaEmpty = isJsonSchemaEmpty(jsonSchemaValue)
    // Drop an empty json_schema so it is not persisted.
    const payloadToSave = isSchemaEmpty
      ? { ...tempPayload, json_schema: undefined }
      : tempPayload
